    "result_text": "All 68 tests pass with **BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`. Verified in the audit logs, e.g. `NSW267D0C08EF1` = `NSW` (region) + `26` (fiscal year) + `7D0C08EF` (HASH8) + `1` (Luhn CHK).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `customerCode` + `checkDigit` schema properties with a single read-only `memberId` property, and removed `membershipNumber`. (DTOs are generated from this spec.)\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Renamed the persisted field/column `customerCode`\u2192`memberId` (`customer_code`\u2192`member_id`) with matching getter/setter. Replaced the instance `getCheckDigit()` (which read `customerCode`) with a reusable static `luhnCheckDigit(String)` helper.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014\n   - Renamed `customerCode(...)`\u2192`memberId(...)`, now composing `region + fy + hash8 + luhnCheckDigit(prefix)`, where FY is the 2-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registration date and HASH8 is the same SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) first-8-upper-hex.\n   - Renamed `deduplicateCustomerCode`\u2192`deduplicateMemberId` so **collision handling now applies to the memberId**.\n   - Updated the human audit line to log `memberId` (dropping `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`), and repointed the structured `OwnerCreatedEvent`'s primary identifier to `memberId`.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Removed the `membershipNumber` mapping; `memberId` now auto-maps by name; `customerCode`/`checkDigit` mappings disappeared with their entity sources. `fiscalYear` is retained.\n\n5. **`Localities.forOwner`** \u2014 Now sources the region from the `memberId` prefix (its leading letter run before the fiscal-year digits) instead of the old `customerCode` dash prefix, with the same city/postcode fallback.\n\n6. **Schema files** (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres) \u2014 Renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` (widened to accommodate the longer format).",
